# PolySniffer Native — Forwarder Lock

Authoritative design: `documentation/architecture/POLYSNIFFER_NATIVE_FORWARDER.md`

## Rule

**Native mode must browse through the forwarder / host-keyed `/pt/polysniff/<host>/` so TrafficLog/HAR capture sees the same traffic a future passthrough handler will proxy.**

Do **not**:

- Launch Playwright / external Chromium as the default Native capture path
- Bypass the proxy so the browser talks to upstream origin directly during Native sniff
- Propose iframes as the default SPA embed

## Success metric

RICH unmodified HAR (cookies, headers, bodies, assets, redirects) while the user walks the normal app flow in the unified workspace UI.

## After enough HAR

Build/refine the app-specific handler (isolation rule). Passthrough + orchestration attach (webhook → consumer) come later. Production Slack events remain API-first mailbox; Native Slack proxy is discovery only.
